      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Sync Interactions",
      "Anchor": "sync-interactions",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "Interactions include any means by which a candidate has interacted with a recruiter, a candidate has interacted with a company, or a recruiter has updated a candidate\u2019s profile within the Talent CRM system (e.g., recruiter tags and notes). All of the interactions that fall into these categories should be sent via the Middleware Platform whenever they are created or updated in your CRM system. When a customer activates CRM Connect for the first time, you must sync all of their historical data to LinkedIn to power the integration.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Prerequisites and Requirements",
      "Anchor": "prerequisites-and-requirements",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Prerequisites and Requirements"
      ],
      "Text": "Query Tunneling -- Requests require query tunneling if the request URL is larger than LinkedIn\u0027s maximum URL length. See Query Tunneling and Migration Guide - Updated API Request Maximum Length for more details.\nCompliance with LinkedIn API Breaking Change Policy\nUsage of the Client Credential Flow (2-legged OAuth) for authentication.\nUsage of the Versioning request format for endpoints and methods that require it as defined in this document.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
